{"ref":"BDB, צָחִיחַ","hw":"צָחִיחַ","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">צָחִיחַ</span>]</big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>shining, glaring, surface</strong> cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">צְחִיחַ סֶלַע</span> i.e. a smooth, bare, rock <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 24:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.24.7\">Ez 24:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 24:8\" href=\"/Ezekiel.24.8\">8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 26:4\" href=\"/Ezekiel.26.4\">26:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 26:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.26.14\">14</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּצְּחִיחִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 4:7\" href=\"/Nehemiah.4.7\">Ne 4:7</a> Qr (Kt <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּצְּחִחִיִים</span>), <em>in glaring, bare places</em> (?).","next":"BDB, צְחִיחָה","prev":"BDB, צַח²"}